From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 11:27:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.65c: UnwindAction::CxxThrowsCleanup variant (1.13 throws
 Phase 1G)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Threads the raw error local through the unwind path for
cxx_throws calls. The MIR pass now sets the Call's unwind
to `CxxThrowsCleanup { bb, raw_err_local }`:

  bb_call:
    call foo(args) -> raw_ok_local   (type: T)
    target → bb_ok_wrap
    unwind → CxxThrowsCleanup { bb: bb_err_wrap, raw_err_local }
  bb_ok_wrap:
    dest = Result::Ok(raw_ok_local)
    goto orig_target
  bb_err_wrap:  (is_cleanup)
    dest = Result::Err(raw_err_local)
    goto orig_target

Codegen's catch BB, when it sees the new variant, stores
the runtime helper's return value into raw_err_local's
stack slot and branches to bb_err_wrap. Replaces the
previous abort-after-catch fallback for the wrapped path.

Touches all visitors of UnwindAction across the compiler:
borrowck, const_eval/miri, codegen_ssa (call + asm),
codegen_llvm (already handled), mir pretty-print, stable
mir conversion, and the mir_transform passes
(add_call_guards, coroutine/drop, elaborate_drops, inline,
validate). For non-cxx_throws paths, the new variant is
treated semantically like UnwindAction::Cleanup.

Bootstrap: clean.
